        <mxCell id="c90" value="&lt;i&gt;Outlined in teal: the three families to buy, only with the crew reduced. In blue: the three to make. In coral: the other three families below the floor, which only need a price. The totals are the path that buys and reprices the rest: an annual effect of 501,792 and one-time costs of 172,660 (severance and tooling); the formula bar adds column C. Two of the three make rows carry no effect, because their families are at or above the floor.&lt;/i&gt;" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;align=left;verticalAlign=top;fontSize=12;fontColor=#5D6D7E;fontStyle=0;fontFamily=Helvetica;spacing=2;fillColor=none;strokeColor=none;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="0" y="630" width="860" height="53" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
